{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And he said to Him.</b> It is puzzling what He is saying, for He had already been appeased, as it is written: ״ויאמר פני ילכו״. And furthermore, what is Moses saying afterward, ״ובמה יודע״ — is it not by Your going with us? For He had already agreed to go with them. One may say that this is what the Holy One, blessed be He, was saying: ״והניחותי לך״ — to you I will grant rest, but not to them, to benefit from the radiance of My Presence. And regarding this Moses said: ״אם אין פניך הולכים״ — if it is the case that they are all like me [that only I receive the Divine Presence], do not bring us up from here. And ״ובמה יודע אפוא״ etc. means: if You go with me and with Your people as at first, by this I shall know that I have found favor in Your eyes. And ״ויאמר ה' אל משה״ etc. means: that I will go with you as at the beginning. Another interpretation: ״פני ילכו״ — My anger will go from Me, and it is like ״ונתתי פני״. And once My anger goes from Me, then ״והניחותי לך״ — but not immediately. ״ויאמר אליו אם אין פניך הולכים״ etc. — for I shall not move from here until You go with us. ״ויאמר גם את הדבר הזה״ etc." "<b>And You have not let me know.</b> At first You said, ״ושלחתי לפניך מלאך״, and in the end You said, ״הורד עדיך״, and still You have not revealed Your intent — whether to go with us or to send an angel — because they took down their ornaments at Your command, and You said, ״ידעתיך בשם״ — that You would make known to me by Name whom You will send with me. And Moses was afraid to pray to HaShem that He go with them, because He had said to him, ״פן אכלך בדרך״. Therefore he said: ״הודיעני נא את דרכיך״ — I shall ask before Him to make known to me His attributes, and according to His attributes I shall know whether it is good for us that He go with us or not, for he did not know how to choose which would be better for them. And the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״פני ילכו״ — I Myself shall go, for this is good for them, and it is like ״ופניך הולכים בקרב״." "<b>And I will grant you rest.</b> From what your heart was troubling you — which you would choose. Even though Moses was still afraid of what He said, ״פן אכלך״, nevertheless he knew that it was the good, for it is glory for Israel that the Holy One, blessed be He, go with them — what He does not do for the other nations. And regarding this he said: ״אם אין פניך הולכים״ etc., ״ונפלינו״ etc. And his mind was still not settled concerning what He said, ״פן אכלך״. The Holy One, blessed be He, said to him: ״גם את הדבר הזה״ etc. — I will make known to you My attributes, and thereby your mind will be settled. And since he saw that it was a time of favor, he added to ask and said: ״הראני נא״ etc. — that is, I want to hear and to see. And He said: ״אני אעביר כל טובי״ — and I will make known to you the attribute of My goodness. ״אעביר״ is in the sense of ״ויעבירו קול במחנה״. ״וקראתי בשם ה' לפניך״ — because he said, ״ואדעך בשם״ — so too I shall do: I shall call before you HaShem, and by that Name I will make known to you that I will go with you."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:47.757290008Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}